# Language (client/MANIFEST.md "Localization"): Options > Interface gets a "Language" row after "Field timers over magic walls and fields" with a button that shows the current language and opens the choice (English, Portugues (Brasil)) of the overlay module client_chaos_locale (ChaosLocale.showMenu). The choice is the module's own setting (g_settings chaos-language), not a client_settings option: no dataset.lua entry, the Ok / Apply of the window do not touch it. Without the module the button hides itself. OTUI only; applies after 0041 (its context is the field timers panel).
--- a/mods/client_settings/options/interface.otui
+++ b/mods/client_settings/options/interface.otui
@@ -396,6 +396,35 @@ InterfaceWindow < Panel
       image-source: /images/skin/show-gui-help-grey
       !tooltip: tr('When checked, the seconds left are shown over magic walls, wild\ngrowth and other timed fields. A field that was already there when it\ncame into view shows "~": its start is not known.')
 
+  FlatPanel
+    size: 505 22
+    anchors.top: prev.bottom
+    anchors.right: parent.right
+    anchors.left: parent.left
+    margin-top: 5
+    margin-left: 4
+    margin-right: 4
+
+    Label
+      id: chaosLanguageLabel
+      !text: tr('Language')
+      font: $var-cip-font
+      color: $var-text-cip-color
+      text-auto-resize: true
+      anchors.left: parent.left
+      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
+      margin-left: 8
+
+    Button
+      id: chaosLanguageButton
+      size: 180 18
+      anchors.right: parent.right
+      anchors.verticalCenter: parent.verticalCenter
+      margin-right: 24
+      !tooltip: tr('The language of the client and of the server messages')
+      @onSetup: if ChaosLocale then self:setText(ChaosLocale.name()) else self:hide() end
+      @onClick: if ChaosLocale then ChaosLocale.showMenu(self) end
+
   FlatPanel
     size: 505 44
     anchors.top: prev.bottom
